WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:04.950
<i>In the year CE 2801,</i>

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:10.540
<i>humanity relocated its political center from 
Earth, the third planet in the Solar System,</i>

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.440
<i>to Theoria, the second planet 
in the Aldebaran Star System...</i>

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.360
<i>and established the Galactic Federation.</i>

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.880
<i>It was declared the first year 
of the Universal Calendar...</i>

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.430
<i>and heralded an era of 
long-lasting growth.</i>

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:25.790
<i>However, this prosperity 
would not last forever.</i>

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:30.250
<i>Humanity was engulfed in the gloom of 
stagnation and uncertainty when,</i>

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.340
<i>in UC 310,</i>

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:39.480
<i>Rudolf Goldenbaum was elected President of 
the Galactic Federation by popular vote.</i>

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.140
<i>The Parliament also named 
him Prime Minister.</i>

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:48.650
<i>In addition, he gave himself the title 
Emperor Rudolf I of the Galactic Empire,</i>

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:55.240
<u>First Emperor of the Galactic Empire
</u>Rudolf von Goldenbaum

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:51.710
<i>at which point the Galactic 
Federation collapsed,</i>

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.990
<i>and the Goldenbaum Dynasty of the 
Galactic Empire was established.</i>

00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:02.160
<i>This made him the first absolute 
monarch of all humanity,</i>

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.970
<i>as well as its dictator.</i>

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.250
<i>Now a holy and inviolable entity,</i>

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:12.400
<i>Rudolf rebuilt the world 
to suit his own ideals.</i>

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:17.180
<i>It was a world in which a subset of 
the nobility ruled the populace.</i>

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:22.180
<i>A widespread outbreak of riots 
followed Rudolf's death,</i>

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.380
<i>but the empire's foundation 
was not shaken.</i>

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:29.000
<i>However, in the year IC 164,</i>

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:30.360
Arle Heinessen

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.360
<i>a group of republicans succeeded 
in escaping the empire's rule.</i>

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.540
<i>After a journey of half a century,</i>

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:40.240
<i>they reached a planet that would 
later be named Heinessen...</i>

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.270
<i>and declared the establishment 
of the Free Planets Alliance.</i>

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.660
<i>Believing themselves to be the true 
heirs of the Galactic Federation,</i>

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.250
<i>they revived the Universal Calendar.</i>

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:58.520
<i>Incidentally, the year UC 527 
coincides with the year IC 218.</i>

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:05.580
<i>The two forces would spend the next 
150 years of their history at war.</i>

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:36.070
<b>Legend of the Galactic Heroes</b>

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:43.980
For your success in subjugating the 
rebel forces in the Astarte Starzone,

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:49.660
I name you, Count Reinhard von Lohengramm, 
the Imperial Fleet Admiral.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:53.490
I also name you Vice Commander 
of the Imperial Space Fleet...

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:58.540
and give you command of 
half of our Space Fleet.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.470
This is the decree of Friedrich IV 
of the Galactic Empire,

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:05.690
given in this, the 487th year 
of the Imperial Calender.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.200
Hmph. A twenty-year-old fleet admiral, eh?

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:34.710
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy Chief Space Fleet Commander
</u>Gregor von Mückenberger

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.740
When did the lustrous Imperial Space Fleet...

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:41.010
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy Armored Grenadier Commander
</u>High Admiral Ovlesser

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:42.000
sink to the level of a child's 
plaything, Your Excellency?

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.130
That blond boy does have tactical skill. 
I can't deny that.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.340
He did defeat the rebels, after all.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:55.350
His talent astonished even the 
seasoned veteran Merkatz.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.040
He does look as if he has lost his bite.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:02.460
He did win, but it may well have 
been an isolated coincidence.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:06.480
If you ask me, it only seems as if 
the enemy was incompetent.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:13.000
<b>Episode 3</b>

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:13.000
<b>An Indomitable Prodigy</b>

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:17.200
Next, his rank will be raised 
from count to marquis.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:21.660
He's done well for himself, even for having 
a sister the kaiser's in love with.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.110
I heard his red-headed flunky is 
getting promoted two ranks, too.

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.320
Don't be shameless!

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.870
Commodore Ansbach!

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:32.640
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy
</u>Commodore Ansbach

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:32.970
Their deeds have made them worthy 
of the ranks they've earned.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:34.620
Watch your tongues.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:35.390
Yes, sir!

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.470
You're being promoted to commodore.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.780
Look forward to it.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:51.170
<i>Every time Reinhard takes 
a step up the ladder,</i>

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:52.730
<i>I'm dragged up behind him.</i>

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:55.900
<i>And at such staggering speed...</i>

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.510
Captain Siegfried Kircheis, correct?

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.740
Yes, and you are?

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:05.690
I'm Captain Paul von Oberstein.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:08.050
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy Captain
</u>Paul von Oberstein

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.810
Pleasure to meet you.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.030
Do you have business with me?

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:14.170
Forgive me.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.890
My artificial eyes seem to be acting up.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.260
I apologize for startling you.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.520
I don't mind.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.560
Did you lose your eyes in battle?

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.670
No, it was a congenital issue.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:30.290
If I had been born in 
Emperor Rudolf's time,

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:34.570
I might have been eliminated under 
the Inferior Genes Exclusion Act.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:39.690
You are blessed with a good superior.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:42.390
There are precious few superior 
officers in the Imperial Army...

00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:45.130
who can make the most of their 
subordinates' abilities.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:47.910
But Count Lohengramm is different.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:52.810
I'm sure it's something those magnates who 
only care about lineage can't fathom.

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:56.260
Which fleet do you serve in?

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:00.930
I was with the intel processing 
division at headquarters,

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:05.810
but I've been appointed to the fleet
at Iserlohn Fortress as a staff officer.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.510
Congratulations.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:15.050
You seem rather guarded.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.720
Salute the fleet admiral!

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.630
I am Captain Paul von Oberstein.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.130
Allow me to offer my congratulations.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.960
I'll be going now.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:33.590
Right.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:35.890
Please excuse me.

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:41.530
Who's he?

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:43.700
A walking enigma, I think.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.140
I see.

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:51.600
He had criticism for 
Emperor Rudolf, did he?

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:55.440
It is always best to remain guarded.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:58.130
Of course, with so many enemies around,

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:00.510
that can be difficult.

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:01.280
Right.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:06.660
I'm seeing my sister tomorrow. 
You'll come along, right?

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:07.960
Are you sure I should?

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:11.540
Of course. Why show restraint now?

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:20.220
<i>Back then, the stars in the 
sky seemed so far from me.</i>

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.180
<i>They were beyond my reach.</i>

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:26.320
<i>I never even considered reaching for them.</i>

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:28.640
<i>And the reason that changed was...</i>

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:30.410
Bye!

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:31.850
See you tomorrow!

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.740
<i>The gate to the house next door is open...</i>

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:49.740
<i>A noble?</i>

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:52.110
<i>Yes, that's what I heard.</i>

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.620
<i>He didn't look like one, though...</i>

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.850
<i>There are many types of nobles.</i>

00:08:56.850 --> 00:09:00.890
Oh, right! The Baldr orchids 
should bloom tomorrow.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:02.730
Wow! Really?

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.030
I'm going now!

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.440
Who are you?

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:33.100
I'm Reinhard von Müsel. Who are you?

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.590
Siegfried... Kircheis.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:42.920
Siegfried? That's a commoner's name.

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:44.570
But...

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:47.680
"Kircheis" is a nice last name.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.450
I like it a lot.

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:52.090
I'll call you by your last name.

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:53.930
You don't mind, do you, Kircheis?

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:54.980
Huh?

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.100
Reinhard?

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:05.530
Sis!

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:08.370
Reinhard, there you are.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.430
Sis, let me introduce you.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:16.430
This is Siegfried Kircheis.

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:18.520
My name is Annerose.

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:22.340
Siegfried... Can I call you "Sieg"?

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:29.310
Sieg, I hope you'll be good 
friends with my brother.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:32.570
I will!

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:35.030
My, you have such energy!

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:40.980
I'll introduce him.

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:43.190
This is Reinhard von Müsel.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:48.340
A kid like him, with "von" in his name?

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:58.420
Man, there's nothing likable 
about that noble kid at all.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:01.010
You're sure you called him out here?

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:02.880
He should show up soon.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:04.810
Let's bust him up nice and quick.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:08.300
Have you seen Reinhard?

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:11.500
Some of the older kids 
asked for him earlier.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:17.690
Reinhard?!

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.390
Bet that taught them a lesson.

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:37.410
This isn't good, though.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.890
If my sister finds out, it'll make her sad.

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:45.970
I have a good idea.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.460
How's that?

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:51.260
Sis!

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:53.650
Have you warmed up a bit?

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:54.230
Yes.

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:56.850
I can't believe you fell in a fountain.

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:59.190
I guess you have a little too much energy.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:04.410
What?

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:07.170
You boys are so strange.

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:12.370
I made a Kelsey plum cake. 
Get dressed and help yourselves.

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.640
Hey, I told you two to get dressed first.

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:24.060
Let's eat!

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.510
By the way, Kircheis,

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:34.000
my sister said she's baking 
another Kelsey plum cake today.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.970
Really? I love those!

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:43.220
That crest...

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.610
Why are they at your house?

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:47.380
Reinhard?

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:50.620
What did you do with Sis?!

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.060
We had no choice.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:56.700
His Highness wanted her.

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:59.160
But this is an honor.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:01.970
You sold her to the kaiser!

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:03.590
You sold my sister!

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:06.110
Reinhard, that's enough!

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.900
The decision has been made.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:20.740
It's all right. It's all right, Reinhard.

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:25.230
This is right.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:48.990
Sieg...

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:54.660
I didn't know you very long, but thank you.

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:58.220
Eat this if you'd like.

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:05.540
Take care of Reinhard for me.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:09.040
Goodbye, Sieg.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:23.400
Kircheis.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:28.480
Reinhard...

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.230
It's been a while.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:31.860
Where were you?!

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:34.590
That uniform...

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:36.480
I joined a cadet school.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.480
Cadet school?

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:41.190
I'll be a soldier.

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:43.410
I can become a real man faster that way.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:47.550
Kircheis, come with me.

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:49.610
To be a soldier?

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:55.090
That's right. We'll get 
my sister back together.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:59.980
Take care of Reinhard for me.

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:19.700
So that's Countess Grünewald's 
younger brother?

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:23.170
Did you hear about the 
red-headed kid? He's a commoner!

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.900
What's a commoner doing here?

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:29.060
He got in because of the 
sister's influence, too.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:32.880
Those two are sons of magnates.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:36.170
They always have servants around 
them to do everything for them.

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:39.090
Can guys like that really 
make it on the battlefield?

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:40.670
They'll never go.

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:45.650
Even if they get into the military, 
most of them get stuck in the rear services.

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:48.470
They have no intention of going out 
and dying on the front lines.

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:51.440
That's how imperial nobles are.

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:01.030
Come on! Run! Run! Run!

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:08.750
Go, go, go, go!

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:09.960
Goal!

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:14.210
Your horse is so slow.

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:15.960
You can say that again. Pathetic.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:17.970
Come on, get up.

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:18.960
You, too.

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:25.480
Those guys didn't earn their 
standing on their own.

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:29.710
There's no reason we should have 
to stand downwind of them.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:33.500
Yeah.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:39.270
Representative of graduating students, Reinhard von Müsel.

00:17:39.270 --> 00:17:40.300
Yes, sir!

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:48.010
Salutatorian, Siegfried Kircheis.

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:48.810
Yes, sir!

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:18.070
Kircheis, have you ever 
thought of it this way?

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:30.370
Sister!

00:18:30.370 --> 00:18:33.190
I'm glad you came, Reinhard.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:34.330
You, too, Sieg.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:38.050
And I am glad to see you 
doing well, Annerose.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:43.810
Annerose von Grünewald

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:40.290
Thank you.

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:44.260
I've been waiting for 
your arrival for days.

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:46.820
Come, let's go inside.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:53.980
<i>She hasn't changed at all since then.</i>

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:57.480
<i>Not even the kaiser himself...</i>

00:18:57.960 --> 00:19:02.080
<i>can do anything to taint these two.</i>

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:05.480
Kircheis.

00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:07.050
Hurry up, now.

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:07.900
Of course.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.860
Have some Kelsey plum cake.

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:17.310
I made it myself, so I don't know 
if it will suit your tastes.

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:19.710
I'll just make my tastes suit it.

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:22.170
Goodness, you're so mean.

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:25.430
It's very good.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:26.920
I'm glad to hear it.

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:32.050
So, Sieg, I'm sure Reinhard has put you 
through all sorts of trouble, right?

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:33.750
No, not at all.

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:35.620
Go on, you can be honest.

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:37.410
Don't tease him!

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:42.440
Oh, right. I also have some delicious 
vin rosé I received as a gift.

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:46.080
I get the picture, Sister.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.370
You want me to go get it, right?

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:52.460
Thank you, Reinhard.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:20:00.430
You have done so much for my brother.

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:05.010
Not at all. He's the one 
who has done much for me.

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:06.590
To be a captain at my age...

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:08.730
It's more than I deserve.

00:20:08.730 --> 00:20:12.310
You'll be a rear admiral 
soon, won't you? I heard.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:13.310
Congratulations.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:16.060
Thank you.

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:23.050
My brother doesn't say it out loud, 
or maybe he just hasn't noticed,

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:25.740
but he truly relies on you a great deal.

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:28.520
You flatter me. I am nothing special.

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:30.730
Sieg...

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:33.730
You should really value 
yourself a bit more.

00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:36.630
My brother has talent,

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:39.890
but he isn't as mature as you.

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:45.390
He's like a wild goat that grows too proud 
of its agility and falls from a cliff,

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:47.480
and he is in a place just as perilous.

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:52.010
So please, Sieg, I ask you...

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:57.040
Watch over Reinhard so that he 
doesn't slip off of that cliff.

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:59.940
If you see him heading in that 
direction, tell him so.

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:04.330
I know he would accept a warning from you.

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.610
I will do everything I can.

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:12.030
Please have faith in my 
loyalty to Reinhard.

00:21:12.470 --> 00:21:16.620
I swear that I will not disappoint you.

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:20.330
Thank you, Sieg.

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:23.530
Annerose...

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:29.120
You should have put it 
someplace easier to find.

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:33.180
Sorry to put you through that, 
but it will be worth the effort.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:35.550
I'll bring the glasses.

00:21:42.620 --> 00:21:44.760
So this is where you went.

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:49.180
I've come this far from that night.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:54.130
Kircheis, have you ever 
thought of it this way?

00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:59.700
The Goldenbaum Dynasty hasn't existed 
since the dawn of humanity.

00:22:00.310 --> 00:22:02.790
It began with this arrogant 
bastard, Rudolf.

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:07.850
Rudolf started out as no more 
than an ambitious upstart,

00:22:08.360 --> 00:22:13.600
but the times were such that he managed 
to become a holy and inviolable emperor.

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:17.100
Hey, Kircheis...

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:23.960
If Rudolf did it, do you think I could?

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:33.230
Reinhard...

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:42.470
Reinhard, please... 
make the universe your own.

00:23:01.430 --> 00:23:02.400
Let's go.

00:23:03.990 --> 00:23:05.630
We shall return to the battlefield.

00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:09.100
Understood.

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Episode 3</b>

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>The Unbeatable Magician</b>

00:24:50.450 --> 00:24:54.830
<i>Next time on </i>Legend of 
 the Galactic Heroes - Die Neue These<i>,</i>

00:24:55.420 --> 00:24:59.070
<i>episode four, "The Unbeatable Magician."</i>
